{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/916689-court-building-and-fae-touched-as-leader","id":916689,"title":"Court Building and Fae Touched as Leader","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-17T23:50:25-07:00","id":916689,"title":"Court Building and Fae Touched as Leader","content":"So, I'm making my own freehold, with the court building that it entails, and I was wondering what kinds of processes in-universe go into making a court. Do Changelings under a single idea/concept band together and the wyrd binds them? Do they form an oath and it becomes greater than the sum of its parts?<br /> <br /> This leads into my other idea: what would happen if a Fae Touched became the Queen/King/leader of the court, possibly by being a founder of it? Naturally it would cause strife among those who come to know it, but what other limitations might this bring? Fae Touched have a wyrd of 0, effectively, but would that hamper their potential?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:09:54-07:00","id":917517,"title":"","content":"I don't think Fae Touched can found courts, just join them.<br /> <br /> But hypothetically one could end up ruling a court, or even made up entirely of Fae Touched.<br /> <br /> Picture this, a Freehold with a large Fae Touched Population, which has joined it courts, and even managed to gain moderate rank in it.<br /> <br /> Then disaster strikes and all the changels are dead, fled, or back in Arcadia, leaving only the Fae Touched.<br /> <br /> By default one of the Fae Touched would have to become the leader of their courts and even one would have to lead the Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T15:48:25-07:00","id":919983,"title":"","content":"I think Freehold based about being ruled by &quot;the meekest&quot; or some other criteria that would make a Fae Touched the most qualified is a very interesting concept. Also it makes a bit of sense that you wouldn't want some uber-powerful demi-god ruling over you if you were Changeling with trauma history of being dominated and humiliated by True Fae masters. Two other things, it'd make the leader a person people actively thought about defending because they wouldn't be able to withstand a magical or physical assault without aid, and that type of relationship would build trust something sorely lacking in many political systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-23-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:00:35-07:00","id":921567,"title":"","content":"The Meek should inherent the earth. Or at leaat the Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T12:44:10-07:00","id":921634,"title":"","content":"The Freehold idea I had was more based around the concept of History, be it living as people used to, living a romanticized version of it, or even avoiding being recognized in history while making it; the idea that prompted the thread was the Court of Bone, one where those who join it examine their own history thoroughly, and use every mistake they made to strengthen themselves. Just as every break in a bone heals stronger, so too will any mistake made strengthen the one who made it. I figured such a concept would be appropriate for a Fae Touched to have come up with, not the least of which being a way for a Fae Touched to justify going into the Hedge more and to try and discover a way to actualize themselves into a proper Changeling.<br /> <br /> Problem is, I'm not sure how courts are actualized in-universe. Is it truly something Changelings can only do, or could a Fae Touched do it, or at least prompt a Changeling/Motley to form it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}